              <h2 class="mt-4 font-athletic text-3xl font-normal italic text-white sm:text-4xl">Feel Stronger</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="chapter-line read-more-content mt-6 max-w-xl text-base leading-8 text-white/62 sm:text-lg" data-read-more-content data-expanded="false">
              <div class="read-more-main" data-read-more-main>
                <p>
                  Enhance your athleticism not by simply 'pushing your limits,' but by building yourself up and becoming a better version of yourself every day.
                  This approach allows you to enjoy training hard without it feeling like a chore, keeping you excited to check in at the gym.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="read-more-expanded" data-read-more-expanded aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="read-more-expanded-text">
                  <p>
                Many people have adopted a gym mentality that says, “Go hard or go home.” Although there may be some truth to it, that does not mean it is the right approach for everyone. For many people, this mindset is not sustainable and often leads to burnout just when they start making progress. As a result, they lose the reward of their hard work and have to start again from zero.
                  </p>
                  <p>
From my experience training in Thailand, we believe in keeping a steady pace. Training should be tiring, but it should still leave you with enough energy to feel good and come back the next day. Repeating this cycle consistently develops both physical and mental strength. No burnout. No unnecessary injuries. No short-term results that disappear quickly.
                  </p>
                  <p>
Some people still compare themselves to others who have already reached the top of the mountain. However, it is important to understand your own body: its limits, strengths, and weaknesses. From there, you follow a program that suits you. That is why we need the guidance of a real trainer.
                  </p>
                </div>
